The treecode source is in ~mswarren/s/tree16

cp -pr ~mswarren/s/tree16 to a suitable location.

Set TREEHOME to point to the location you just moved
the source to (i.e. setenv TREEHOME ~/s/tree16)

If you want to rebuild the binary
cd $TREEHOME
rm -rf Objfiles */Objfiles
On an Origin 2000, build the program by typing "make ARCH=O2k PAROS=mpi"
If that doesn't work, make sure you are using GNU make

The binary ends up in $TREEHOME/relerr/relerr.O2k-mpi

Execute with (for example):

cd $TREEHOME/relerr
mpirun -np 32 relerr.O2k-mpi test10Mnln.ctl

That will run a 10 million particle problem, which takes somewhat less
than 2 Gbytes of memory.

One can adjust nsteps in the .ctl file to take more steps, or nobj to
run a bigger problem, or make errtol larger to compute forces less
accurately (to take less time).

